  "unverified_facts": [
    "Leopard seals (Hydrurga leptonyx) reach about 3.5 m (11 ft) and close to 500 kg; females are larger than males.",
    "Their cheek teeth are three-pointed and interlock to sieve krill from the water.",
    "Leopard seals ambush penguins near the ice edge where they enter and leave the water.",
    "They also eat fish, squid and young seals of other species.",
    "Photographer Paul Nicklen reported a female leopard seal repeatedly bringing him penguins.",
    "In 2003 a leopard seal killed marine biologist Kirsty Brown at Rothera; it is the only recorded human fatality.",
    "Leopard seals use sea ice for resting, breeding and molting."
